# Backblaze B2 credentials for backup/archivebox-backup.sh. Copy to
# backup/b2.env ON THE VPS and fill in -- never commit the filled-in file
# (backup/b2.env is gitignored; this repo is public).
#
# Setup that makes the off-box copy actually resist a VPS compromise:
#   - bucket with Object Lock ENABLED and a DEFAULT RETENTION of 90 days in
#     compliance mode -- that is what makes uploads undeletable by anyone,
#     including a key that has deleteFiles
#   - application key restricted to that ONE bucket ("Allow List All Bucket
#     Names" ticked -- rclone needs it). The web console's Read and Write
#     preset includes deleteFiles; with compliance retention that is harmless.
#     Optionally recreate the key via the B2 CLI without deleteFiles.
#   - the script only ever `rclone copy`s -- never sync, never delete
# Step-by-step with console navigation: backup/B2-SETUP.md
RCLONE_CONFIG_B2_TYPE=b2
RCLONE_CONFIG_B2_ACCOUNT=REPLACE_ME_keyID
RCLONE_CONFIG_B2_KEY=REPLACE_ME_applicationKey
B2_BUCKET=REPLACE_ME_bucket_name
